 "response": "Stedamu's budget is now **$2503K**.\n\n**How it was worked out:**\n- Under the policy, only Finance Office entries count. All Engineering, Vendor, PMO, Sales, Legal, Marketing, Operations and Facilities messages were ignored, as were Finance Office notes that don't change the budget (audits, reminders, archived batches and similar).\n- I followed each chain of withdrawals to its end. A withdrawal counts only if it was not itself withdrawn. When a withdrawal is withdrawn, the original update counts again. Some examples:\n  - #0002 (\u2212$36K) counts. The chain is #0003 \u2192 #0007 \u2192 #0078 \u2192 #0112 \u2192 #0439 \u2192 #0632, and it ends with #0003 cancelled.\n  - #0010 (\u2212$407K) is removed. #1367 cancels #0845, which brings back #0175. #0175 cancels #0057, so #0013's withdrawal of #0010 stands.\n  - #0014 (+$556K) counts, because #0270 cancels the withdrawal in #0019.\n  - #1423 (\u2212$206K) counts, because #1544 cancels the withdrawal in #1522.\n- Starting from the $1880K set in #0001, I applied each remaining increase and decrease once, in record order. The last ones are #1597 (+$75K) and #1598 (+$5K), giving $2503K.\n\nANSWER: $2503K",
